/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Analysis Signal analysis
 * @ingroup DspCore
 * @brief Stateless block measurements and stateful streaming level estimators.
 *
 * Include `<DspCore_Analysis.h>` or Block.h/Streaming.h individually.
 * All operations use the selected float/double precision. Block measurements
 * and streaming updates allocate nothing; Streaming::MovingRMS allocates its
 * fixed history only in Configure.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Analysis_Block Block measurements
 *
 * - **SPEC-ANA-1**: Block::Peak and Block::RMS accept a read-only Processing::SampleBlock.
 *   They require a valid view and finite samples; failure leaves output
 *   unchanged. Empty blocks, including nullptr with zero count, produce zero.
 *   The caller guarantees accessible input extent. Output may alias an input
 *   sample: it is committed only after all reads finish.
 * - **SPEC-ANA-2**: Peak returns maximum absolute amplitude. RMS includes DC
 *   and measures only the supplied block; it is not a sliding or accumulating
 *   window. RMS scales by peak before squaring, avoiding overflow for maximum
 *   finite signals and retaining small signals. Normalized roundoff is bounded
 *   at one before rescaling, reflecting the mathematical RMS<=peak bound.
 *   Reductions use the selected precision; large-block rounding remains its
 *   normal limitation. No mean removal, dB conversion or loudness weighting
 *   is hidden in either measurement.
 *
 * For a block @f$x[0],\ldots,x[N-1]@f$, Peak evaluates
 * @f[
 * P = \max_{0\leq n<N}\left|x[n]\right|.
 * @f]
 * RMS evaluates @f$R=0@f$ when @f$P=0@f$. Otherwise it uses the algebraically
 * equivalent, overflow-resistant form
 * @f[
 * R = P\sqrt{\min\left(1,\frac{1}{N}
 *     \sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\left(\frac{x[n]}{P}\right)^2\right)}.
 * @f]
 *
 * @section DspCore_Analysis_Streaming Streaming estimators
 *
 * - **SPEC-ANA-3**: Streaming::EnvelopeFollower rectifies each sample and applies a
 *   one-pole smoother with attack when magnitude>current value, release
 *   otherwise. Configure takes nonnegative finite time constants in seconds
 *   and preserves value. Default zero times snap immediately to magnitude.
 *   Reset accepts a finite nonnegative initial amplitude. Update requires
 *   finite sample and positive finite dt in seconds; failure preserves state
 *   and output. No sample clock or rate is inferred.
 * - **SPEC-ANA-4**: One-pole alpha=1-exp(-dt/tau) uses a stable small-ratio
 *   series and a snap at ratios >=40. No global denormal mode is changed.
 *   State is a trivially copyable three-scalar object with target size budgets.
 *
 * Let @f$m[n]=|x[n]|@f$ and choose @f$\tau@f$ as attack when
 * @f$m[n]>v[n-1]@f$, otherwise release. For a positive interval @f$\Delta t@f$,
 * the follower evaluates
 * @f[
 * \alpha = 1-e^{-\Delta t/\tau}, \qquad
 * v[n] = v[n-1] + \alpha\bigl(m[n]-v[n-1]\bigr).
 * @f]
 * A zero time constant selects @f$\alpha=1@f$, so the state snaps to
 * @f$m[n]@f$. The implementation evaluates the small-ratio limit with a series
 * rather than subtracting nearly equal floating-point values.
 *
 * Streaming::MovingRMS retains a fixed ring of squared samples and one running
 * sum. Each Update removes the oldest square, adds the new one and returns one
 * exact RMS value. It uses partial-window normalization until IsReady reports
 * that the configured window is full. Configure allocates its history; Update
 * and Reset do not allocate.
 * For a window containing @f$M@f$ available samples, it evaluates
 * @f[
 * R[n]=\sqrt{\frac{1}{M}\sum_{k=0}^{M-1}x[n-k]^2}.
 * @f]
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * DspCore::Analysis::Streaming::MovingRMS<float> rms;
 * if (!rms.Configure(256U)) return;
 *
 * float level{};
 * if (!rms.Update(inputSample, level)) return;
 * const bool windowIsFull = rms.IsReady();
 * @endcode
 *
 * The follower is an amplitude follower rather than RMS detection or a
 * synthesizer envelope generator. Examples: Analysis/Levels and Analysis/Envelope.
 * See @ref DspCore_Generators_Envelopes for generated segments.
 */
/** @namespace DspCore::Analysis
 * @brief Signal analysis split into Block measurements and Streaming estimators.
 */
/** @namespace DspCore::Analysis::Block
 * @brief Stateless measurements over a complete SampleBlock.
 */
/** @namespace DspCore::Analysis::Streaming
 * @brief Stateful processors that emit one estimate for every input sample.
 */
